"\n\n\n\n\n## Review\nThere was a time when I was into lucid dreaming when I was younger.  \nI felt that sleeping time was a waste and wanted to sleep as late as possible or utilize the sleeping time.  \nSo I had a lot of interest in sleep and read this book without getting bored.  \n\nThis book brings a shift in thinking that sleep is not a waste of life, but an opportunity to experience another life. The author uses actual scientific theories such as the five stages of sleep, REM sleep, brain science, and psychology as the skeleton of the story, and adds mystical imagination such as , , and  to draw the reader into the unknown world of sleep.  \nThe , a characteristic of Werber's novels, appears in this work as well without fail.  "